belief-update],\n     :rules-not-in-the-cascade [],\n     :then-correspondence\n     [{:encodes\n       \"\\\"Search the library on every turn as a background process.\\\"\",\n       :encoding-limit\n       \"the THEN also says to display results, log the activation history, and tune retrieval from hot/cold zones. The zaif arm set has no term for any of those, so this rule encodes the search clause only and the rest is unencodable rather than encoded.\",\n       :then-source\n       \"war-machine/ambient-pattern-retrieval.flexiarg:16-16\",\n       :rule :aif/no-self-certification,\n       :span-inside-the-then-block? true,\n       :pattern-id-matches-path? false,\n       :then-block [15 18],\n       :span-is-non-empty? true,\n       :counterfactual? false,\n       :file-exists? true}\n      {:encodes\n       \"\\\"Search once more against the installed source ... and look for an adapter to an existing theorem before building\\\"; \\\"Put exactly one `sorry` at the observed gap ... Beside that `sorry`, leave the consultation trail\\\"; \\\"stop researching once the misses repeat\\\"\",\n       :encoding-limit nil,\n       :then-source\n       \"math-strategy/missing-dependency-protocol.flexiarg:59-77\",\n       :rule :math-strategy/missing-dependency-protocol,\n       :span-inside-the-then-block? false,\n       :pattern-id-matches-path? true,\n       :then-block [59 79],\n       :span-is-non-empty? true,\n       :counterfactual? false,\n       :file-exists? true}\n      {:encodes\n       \"\\\"When budget nears exhaustion, force a decision: commit to best-so-far, escalate to a supervisor, or explicitly expand scope with justification.\\\"\",\n       :encoding-limit\n       \"the THEN offers three terminal choices -- commit to best-so-far, escalate to a supervisor, expand scope with justification -- and asks for reset rules. The zaif arm set has a term for none of the three: :yield is the nearest to `commit to best-so-far`, :ask is the nearest to `escalate`, and nothi